message: "If you use FlowMate in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "FlowMate: free, open-source flow cytometry analysis in the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Harel"
    given-names: "Shir"
    email: "rlshir302010@gmail.com"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rlshir302010-cpu/flowmate"
url: "https://rlshir302010-cpu.github.io/flowmate/"
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - gating
  - FCS
  - compensation
  - FlowJo workspace
  - bioinformatics
  - open source
abstract: >-
  FlowMate is a browser-based flow cytometry analysis application. It reads FCS 2.0–3.1 files,
  gates every well of a plate at once (polygon, rectangle, ellipse, quadrant, range and Boolean
  gates), compensates with file, computed or imported matrices, imports FlowJo 10 workspaces and
  Gating-ML 2.0, and reports per-condition statistics (t tests, one-way ANOVA with Tukey or Dunnett,
  and nested mixed-model tests for cell-level data). All processing happens locally in the browser.
  Results are validated against FlowKit, Beckman CytExpert, GraphPad Prism and R on public data.
